    ci: reduce GPU usage and parallelize test setup (#3944)
    
    Reduce CI time and GPU usage by selecting the relevant test suites for
    each PR, moving hosted eval to CPU, and running independent setup steps
    in parallel.
    
    - Select GPU unit tests, SFT, RL, and hosted eval from changed paths
    before allocating runners. Shared runtime and dependency changes retain
    broad coverage; pushes to `main` and manual runs execute the full suite.
    - Keep RL/SFT coverage for checkpoint converters, dashboard code, and
    the shared dashboard smoke helper.
    - Run `gsm8k_eval` on `ubuntu-latest` because it uses hosted inference.
    - Run public submodule initialization and `uv` setup concurrently, then
    wait for both before installing dependencies. Keep dependency caching
    keyed on `uv.lock` and the five-job limit on GPU integration tests.
    - Cancel superseded CPU and style runs on the same PR.
    - Give the GPU workflow read-only contents access and the test selector
    PR read access.
    
    <!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->
    ---
    
    > [!NOTE]
    > **Medium Risk**
    > Path-based GPU job gating can skip integration coverage on PRs if
    filters miss a dependency; full suite still runs on main and manual
    dispatch.
    >
    > **Overview**
    > **GPU CI now picks which jobs to run from the PR diff**, instead of
    always running the full GPU unit + integration matrix on every non-draft
    PR. A new **Select tests** job uses path filters for unit, SFT, RL, and
    eval; pushes to `main` and `workflow_dispatch` still run everything.
    RL/SFT integration scenarios are built dynamically (still capped at
    `max-parallel: 5` on `prime-rl-2xh200`).
    >
    > **`gsm8k_eval` is split out** into a dedicated job on `ubuntu-latest`
    (hosted inference), so it no longer consumes GPU runners. Integration
    pytest invocations use `tests/integration/test_${{ matrix.test }}.py`
    from the dynamic matrix rather than per-row `pytest_args`.
    >
    > **Setup and queueing tweaks:** submodule init and `setup-uv` run in
    parallel in CPU/GPU jobs; CPU and style workflows cancel in-progress
    runs per PR; GPU workflow gets `workflow_dispatch`, read-only
    `contents`, and PR-scoped concurrency cancel. `docs/development.md`
    documents the new triggers and runner split.
    >
    > <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit
    20da35f30de85b2b18cf82e29598846a1228ca12. Bugbot is set up for automated
    code reviews on this repo. Configure
    [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>
